<speak>Checking the diary at home sounds more comfortable than making a hurried arrangement from the office. When you contact us about a future appointment, a couple of possible windows would be enough for ordinary scheduling. You do not need to describe the rest of the family's plans. We can work from the availability you give us. If a routine call ever reaches you at an inconvenient moment, you can simply say so; there is no expectation that you should stop whatever you are doing. We would rather arrange a proper conversation than have you half listening while managing several other things.</speak>